## SUMMARY

<span lang="ja">Textus/CNCFは、CMLのモデルとCNCFの標準機能を使う通常の開発から、認可、整合性、リアクティブな実行、観測などの共通機構を利用できるようにしています。本書は、非機能要求と品質属性を起点に、技術の組合せによる効果、基盤と開発者の分担、用途に応じた構成と確認を説明します。</span><span lang="en">Textus/CNCF makes shared authorization, consistency, reactive execution, and observation available through ordinary development with CML models and standard CNCF facilities. This guide starts from non-functional requirements and quality attributes to explain combined effects, infrastructure and developer responsibilities, and application-specific configuration and verification.</span>

# Expressing Non-functional Requirements through Qualities and Conditions｜非機能要求を品質属性と利用条件へ具体化する

<span lang="ja">機能要求が「何を行うか」を示すのに対し、非機能要求は、その機能をどのような負荷、障害、利用環境、運用条件の下で提供するかを示します。性能、可用性、セキュリティ、変更容易性などの品質属性は、その要求を整理する観点です。非機能要求には費用や配備環境などの制約も含まれ、複数の品質を合わせて満たす構成を選びます。</span><span lang="en">Functional requirements describe what a system does. Non-functional requirements describe the load, failures, usage environments, and operating conditions under which it must provide that functionality. Quality attributes such as performance, availability, security, and modifiability provide perspectives for organizing these requirements. Cost and deployment constraints also influence the combination of qualities to support.</span>

<span lang="ja">「速い」「止まらない」だけでは、必要な構成を選べません。対象の操作、要求や障害の発生源、発生する事象、負荷などの条件、期待する応答、確認する尺度を定めます。例えば長時間処理では、受付までの時間と処理完了までの時間を分け、障害後には、許容する停止時間と失ってよいデータの範囲を分けます。これは品質属性シナリオによる要求の具体化に対応します。参考：SEI Quality Attribute Workshops, Third Edition（https://www.sei.cmu.edu/documents/716/2003_005_001_14249.pdf）。</span><span lang="en">Terms such as fast or always available do not select an architecture. Define the affected operation, source and event, conditions such as load, expected response, and response measure. For long-running work, distinguish time to acceptance from time to completion. For recovery, distinguish tolerable downtime from tolerable data loss. This follows the quality attribute scenario approach. Reference: SEI Quality Attribute Workshops, Third Edition (https://www.sei.cmu.edu/documents/716/2003_005_001_14249.pdf).</span>

