| <span lang="ja">運用容易性・資源効率・費用</span><span lang="en">Operability / resource efficiency / cost</span> | <span lang="ja">標準設定＋容量・常駐範囲・保持期間の調整＋共通運用</span><span lang="en">Defaults + capacity/residency/retention settings + common operations</span> | <span lang="ja">個別設定と実装を減らし、必要な水準に資源を配分する</span><span lang="en">Reduce bespoke setup and allocate resources to required levels</span> |

# Connecting Models and Components to Shared Execution｜モデルと部品を共通の実行経路へ接続する

<span lang="ja">CMLは、Entityを基盤とするAggregate・View、状態機械を基盤とするWorkflow、業務規則と公開Operationを定義します。実行可能なモデルはTextusが直接実行し、Cozyは型付きAPIや接続構造を生成します。モデルにある意味と制約をコードや画面ごとに再実装する範囲が減り、業務規則と実行時の操作を対応付けられます。</span><span lang="en">CML defines Aggregates and Views based on Entities, Workflows based on state machines, business rules, and public Operations. Textus directly executes executable models, while Cozy generates typed APIs and connecting structures. This reduces repeated implementation of model semantics and constraints in code and screens, connecting business rules to runtime operations.</span>

<span lang="ja">CBDは、各コンポーネントの責務と公開契約を定めます。外部との接点をAPIとSPIへ集め、内部のデータ操作や外部作用をUoWの経路へ接続することで、独立した部品を共通の認可・確定・資源管理の下で動かします。部品の独立性だけでなく、その部品をどこで再利用しても同じ実行上の扱いへ接続できることが、品質の維持に寄与します。</span><span lang="en">CBD defines component responsibilities and public contracts. APIs and SPIs define external contacts, while data operations and external effects connect to the UoW path. Independent components thereby run under shared authorization, commit, and resource management. Quality benefits come both from component independence and from reconnecting reused components to the same runtime controls.</span>

<span lang="ja">[[images/execution-boundaries-ja.png]]</span><span lang="en">[[images/execution-boundaries-en.png]]</span>

<span lang="ja">図1　モデルから接続された業務処理が通る共通の実行境界。認可、更新の確定、資源の終了を同じ経路で扱います。</span><span lang="en">Figure 1. Shared execution boundaries for model-connected business operations: authorization, commit, and resource termination.</span>

<span lang="ja">型と純粋関数型の合成は、入力・出力と接続できる処理を明示します。Consequence／Conclusionは成功・失敗とその情報を揃え、Free Monadによる操作記述をUoWの実行へ渡します。複雑な制御を補完コードへ埋め込む範囲を減らすため、AIが作成した処理も共通基盤の管理へ接続しやすくなります。型による検査と実行時の管理は、異なる範囲の誤りを扱う仕組みとして組み合わせます。</span><span lang="en">Types and pure functional composition make inputs, outputs, and valid connections explicit. Consequence/Conclusion standardize outcomes and failure information, while Free Monad operation descriptions pass to UoW execution. Reducing controls embedded in supplementary code also makes AI-written processing easier to connect to shared runtime management. Type checks and runtime controls address different classes of errors and work together.</span>

# Managing Asynchronous Benefits and Complexity in the Runtime｜非同期化の利点と複雑性を実行基盤で扱う

<span lang="ja">リアクティブな構成では、メッセージによって処理間の時間的な依存を減らし、負荷の分散、実行数の調整、障害の隔離を組み合わせます。リアクティブ宣言の応答性、耐障害性、弾力性、メッセージ駆動は、この関係を整理した四つの特性です。非同期化に負荷制御と回復を組み合わせることが、性能、可用性、柔軟性への効果につながります。参考：リアクティブ宣言（https://www.reactivemanifesto.org/ja）。</span><span lang="en">Reactive architecture uses messages to reduce temporal dependencies, combined with load distribution, capacity adjustment, and failure isolation. The Reactive Manifesto organizes this relationship through responsiveness, resilience, elasticity, and message-driven communication. Combining asynchronous processing with load control and recovery supports performance, availability, and flexibility. Reference: The Reactive Manifesto (https://www.reactivemanifesto.org/).</span>

<span lang="ja">非同期処理では、順序、完了、再試行、重複、データの鮮度を扱う必要があります。Textus/CNCFは、Job／Task、状態機械、Workflow、UoW、イベントと共通の結果表現を接続し、これらを管理する経路を用意します。開発者がモデルと標準機能に沿って実装すると、この経路で処理が実行されるため、スケジューラや進行管理を業務処理ごとに作る必要を減らせます。リアクティブ性の実現に必要な技術的な複雑さを基盤へ委ねる構成です。</span><span lang="en">Asynchronous processing must handle ordering, completion, retries, duplicates, and data freshness. Textus/CNCF connects Jobs/Tasks, state machines, Workflows, UoW, events, and common outcome semantics to provide managed execution paths. Implementations using models and standard facilities run through these paths, reducing the need for application-specific schedulers and progress management. The architecture delegates the technical complexity of reactive execution to the infrastructure.</span>

<span lang="ja">[[images/tier-lifetimes-ja.png]]</span><span lang="en">[[images/tier-lifetimes-en.png]]</span>

<span lang="ja">図2　要求の受付、長時間処理、業務状態、永続状態の分担。受付と完了、処理の進行と更新の確定を区別します。</span><span lang="en">Figure 2. Responsibilities for admission, long-running work, business state, and persistence. Acceptance differs from completion, and progression differs from commit.</span>

<span lang="ja">Application tierの伸縮は、Domain tierとDataStoreの容量に合わせます。DomainではWorking SetとViewで取得の負担を減らし、AggregateとUoWで更新を管理します。参照を高速化する場合も、更新の確定とViewへの反映を区別し、必要な鮮度を定めます。処理能力、応答時間、整合性を同じ実行経路の上で調整することが、個別の高速化とは異なるアーキテクチャ上の効果です。</span><span lang="en">Application scaling is coordinated with Domain and DataStore capacity. Working Sets and Views reduce loading, while Aggregates and UoW manage updates. Faster reads still require distinguishing committed updates from View refresh and defining acceptable freshness. Coordinating capacity, latency, and consistency along the same execution path provides a system-level effect beyond isolated optimizations.</span>

# Applying Protection, Consistency, and Traceability to the Same Operation｜保護・整合性・追跡を一つの操作へ適用する

<span lang="ja">Presentation tierは、Web、Flutter、外部の独自UIなどで構成でき、サーバー側の信頼の前提には置きません。Application tierが要求を調整し、Domain tierの公開Operationを呼び出します。標準経路では、共通の認証文脈を引き継ぎ、Operationの認可に加えて、対象Entityと利用資源の条件を確認します。SimpleEntityの所有者・グループなどの基本情報とUNIX型のread／write権限を共通に扱うことで、部品ごとの独自実装を減らします。</span><span lang="en">The Presentation tier may use Web, Flutter, or an independently built UI and is not a server-side trust assumption. The Application tier coordinates requests and invokes public Domain Operations. Standard execution carries a shared authenticated context and checks Operation authorization as well as access to target Entities and resources. Common SimpleEntity ownership/group information and UNIX-style read/write permissions reduce independent implementations in each component.</span>

<span lang="ja">許可された操作も、Aggregateの不変条件、状態機械の遷移条件、UoWの確定処理に従います。基盤が収集する実行記録と監査証跡を同じ操作や対象へ関連付けると、何が許可され、何が確定し、どこで失敗したかを確認できます。保護の判定、更新管理、観測を同じ経路へ置くことで、認可されたが更新結果を追えない、といった分断を減らします。</span><span lang="en">Authorized operations still follow Aggregate invariants, state-machine transition rules, and UoW commit handling. Relating infrastructure-collected execution records and audit trails to the same operation and target shows what was permitted, what committed, and where failure occurred. Keeping protection decisions, update management, and observation on shared paths reduces gaps between authorization and traceable outcomes.</span>

<span lang="ja">通常の開発では、CMLの定義と基本設定を標準経路へ接続し、業務ごとに保護や記録の機構を実装する負担を減らします。誰に何を許可するか、監査記録をどれだけ保存するかは用途の条件です。より強い区画分離や機能制限が必要な場合は、配備構成とCapabilityの制限を組み合わせます。共通の基本機構を起点に、必要な範囲を追加する分担です。</span><span lang="en">Ordinary development connects CML definitions and basic settings to standard paths, reducing bespoke protection and recording code. Who may perform which operations and how long audit records are kept remain application requirements. Stronger isolation or functional restrictions combine deployment choices with Capability restrictions. Shared basic mechanisms provide the starting point for additional requirements.</span>

# Expanding Functionality and User Platforms while Preserving Contracts｜業務契約を保ちながら変更と利用環境を広げる

<span lang="ja">機能拡張の柔軟性は、処理能力の拡張とは別の品質です。CMLから得られる型付きAPIとComponent／Service／Operationの契約を利用すると、既存部品を再利用し、必要な接続コードを契約に沿って作れます。外部サービスや保存方式をSPIの実装側へ分けることで、接続先の変更が業務モデルへ及ぶ範囲を抑えます。モデル検査、コンパイル、CARの検査、部品のレビューを組み合わせると、変更した契約と実装の不一致を異なる段階で確認できます。</span><span lang="en">Functional extensibility differs from capacity scalability. Typed APIs derived from CML and Component/Service/Operation contracts support component reuse and contract-guided connecting code. Keeping external services and storage mechanisms behind SPIs limits provider changes reaching business models. Model checks, compilation, CAR inspection, and component review examine contract/implementation mismatches at different stages.</span>

<span lang="ja">Viewは参照結果の意味を、Displayは表示への投影を担い、更新は公開Operationへ戻します。この分担を使って標準Web UIやTextusと連動するFlutterアプリケーションを構成すると、業務規則を共有しながらスマートフォン、タブレット、Web、Desktopへ展開できます。RESTやgRPCで独自UIを接続する構成も、公開契約とサーバー側の保護を共有する考え方です。表示技術を選択できることと、業務操作の一貫性を保つことを両立させます。</span><span lang="en">Views preserve read-result semantics, Displays project them for presentation, and updates return through public Operations. Standard Web UI or Textus-connected Flutter applications can use this division to share business rules across phones, tablets, Web, and Desktop. Independently built UIs connected through REST or gRPC follow the same principle of public contracts and server-side protection. Presentation choice can therefore coexist with consistent business operations.</span>

<span lang="ja">使用性には、処理が受け付けられたか、完了したか、入力を直す必要があるかを利用者が理解できることも含まれます。共通の入力検査、Consequence／Conclusion、Jobの進行情報を画面へ対応付けると、状態や失敗の意味を揃えられます。画面寸法、入力手段、アクセシビリティなどの利用条件は、対象のUIで確認します。共通モデルは意味の一貫性を支え、具体的な使いやすさはその意味を利用者へどう提示するかで決まります。</span><span lang="en">Usability includes understanding whether work was accepted or completed and whether input needs correction. Mapping common input validation, Consequence/Conclusion, and Job progress to the UI provides consistent meanings for state and failure. Screen sizes, input methods, and accessibility are checked in the target UI. Shared models support semantic consistency; practical usability also depends on how those semantics are presented.</span>

# Starting with Standard Configuration and Adjusting Required Levels｜標準構成を起点に必要な水準へ調整する

<span lang="ja">標準のモデルと機能を使うことは、品質対策を適用する経路を選ぶことでもあります。開発者は業務の意味を定め、基盤は共通の制御を実行します。処理量、可用性、保持期間などの目標に応じて設定と配備を調整し、業務固有の補償や認可を指定します。用途に必要な条件を決めることと、その条件を適用する機構を自前で開発することを分けることで、導入と運用を簡単にします。</span><span lang="en">Using standard models and facilities also selects the paths that apply quality controls. Developers define business meaning, and the runtime executes common controls. Configuration and deployment adjust throughput, availability, and retention, while business-specific compensation and authorization are specified separately. Separating the choice of application conditions from building their enforcement mechanisms simplifies adoption and operation.</span>

<span lang="ja">品質属性は独立には決まりません。メモリ常駐を増やすと取得時間を減らせる一方、メモリ費用と再構築時間に影響します。参照を非同期に更新すると応答性を高めやすい一方、鮮度の条件が必要です。冗長化や強い区画分離は可用性や保護を支えますが、配備と運用の費用を増やします。求める水準に合わせてこれらを組み合わせ、標準機構の再利用で個別実装と確認の負担を抑えます。</span><span lang="en">Quality attributes interact. More resident data can reduce retrieval time while affecting memory cost and reconstruction time. Asynchronous read-model updates can improve responsiveness while requiring freshness rules. Redundancy and stronger isolation support availability and protection but add deployment and operating costs. Select combinations for the required levels and reuse standard mechanisms to reduce bespoke implementation and verification.</span>

#+CAPTION: <span lang="ja">基盤と開発・運用の分担</span><span lang="en">Infrastructure and application responsibilities</span>
| <span lang="ja">対象</span><span lang="en">Concern</span> | <span lang="ja">共通基盤が担うこと</span><span lang="en">Shared infrastructure</span> | <span lang="ja">開発・運用で定めること</span><span lang="en">Development/operations choices</span> |
| --- | --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">業務データと進行</span><span lang="en">Business data and progression</span> | <span lang="ja">モデル操作、遷移、更新の確定</span><span lang="en">Model operations, transitions, and commit</span> | <span lang="ja">不変条件、許された遷移、参照の鮮度</span><span lang="en">Invariants, allowed transitions, read freshness</span> |
| <span lang="ja">非同期実行</span><span lang="en">Asynchronous execution</span> | <span lang="ja">受付・進行・結果の管理、資源の管理</span><span lang="en">Admission/progress/outcome and resource management</span> | <span lang="ja">直接／Jobの選択、処理量、業務固有の再試行・補償</span><span lang="en">Direct/Job selection, workload, business retries/compensation</span> |
| <span lang="ja">保護と監査</span><span lang="en">Protection and audit</span> | <span lang="ja">認証文脈、操作・対象の認可、記録</span><span lang="en">Authenticated context, operation/data checks, records</span> | <span lang="ja">利用する認証方式、権限規則、記録の保持と閲覧</span><span lang="en">Authentication method, permissions, retention/access</span> |
| <span lang="ja">可用性と回復</span><span lang="en">Availability and recovery</span> | <span lang="ja">選択した構成での切替え・再構築の経路</span><span lang="en">Failover/reconstruction paths in selected configurations</span> | <span lang="ja">障害の想定、冗長化範囲、復旧時間と費用</span><span lang="en">Failure assumptions, redundancy scope, recovery time/cost</span> |
| <span lang="ja">表示と接続</span><span lang="en">Presentation and integration</span> | <span lang="ja">共通の業務・表示契約と接続点</span><span lang="en">Shared business/presentation contracts and extension points</span> | <span lang="ja">UI基盤、外部サービス、利用環境</span><span lang="en">UI platform, external services, usage environments</span> |

<span lang="ja">モデルと型の検査では、規則や接続の不一致を確認します。実行時には、対象の負荷での応答、障害時の確定状態と回復、許可・拒否と監査記録を確認します。相関情報で受付、Operation、Job／Task、UoWの記録をつなぐと、待機、処理、再試行のどこで目標との差が生じたかを調べられます。結果をモデル・設定・配備の調整へ戻し、同じ条件で確認する流れにします。</span><span lang="en">Model and type checks detect inconsistent rules and connections. Runtime checks cover responses under representative load, committed state and recovery after failure, and authorization decisions with audit records. Correlating admission, Operation, Job/Task, and UoW records identifies whether gaps arise in waiting, execution, or retries. Feed findings back into models, configuration, and deployment and recheck under the same conditions.</span>

<span lang="ja">本書はTextus/CNCFの技術体系と責務分担をまとめています。利用時には採用する版の実装範囲を各専門ガイドで確認します。永続Jobの再開、可用性Profileと交代経路、用途別セキュリティProfileや運用手順、UIの生成経路などには設計・整備中の項目もあります。標準機構による支援と、対象環境で確認した性能や可用性の水準は分けて記録します。</span><span lang="en">This guide describes the technology system and its division of responsibilities. Consult the specialist guides for the implementation scope of the selected version. Durable Job resumption, availability profiles and replacement paths, security profiles and operating procedures, and some UI generation paths include work still under design or development. Record infrastructure support separately from performance and availability levels verified in the target environment.</span>

# Conclusion｜まとめ

<span lang="ja">Textus/CNCFは、CMLのモデル、コンポーネントの契約、共通の実行機構を組み合わせ、品質対策を通常の開発と運用の経路へ組み込みます。開発者は業務に必要な条件をモデルと設定へ表し、複雑な実行制御を基盤へ委ねます。標準的な作法で作ることが複数の品質対策の利用につながり、用途に応じた構成と確認によって必要な水準へ調整できることが、このアーキテクチャの効果です。</span><span lang="en">Textus/CNCF combines CML models, component contracts, and shared runtime mechanisms to place quality controls on ordinary development and operating paths. Developers express business conditions in models and configuration and delegate complex execution controls to the infrastructure. Following standard conventions connects applications to multiple quality mechanisms, while application-specific configuration and verification establish the required levels.</span>

# Related Technical Guides and References｜関連技術ガイドと参考資料

<span lang="ja">各機構の詳しい説明は、次の技術ガイドに分担します。これらは本リポジトリ内の関連資料です。品質属性から全体を読む場合は本書を入口とし、実装やモデルの詳細は対応するガイドで確認できます。</span><span lang="en">The following guides provide detailed explanations of individual mechanisms. They are related documents in this repository. This guide provides a quality-oriented entry point; model and implementation details belong to the corresponding specialist guides.</span>

<span lang="ja">品質属性シナリオの参考資料は、SEI「Quality Attribute Workshops, Third Edition」（https://www.sei.cmu.edu/documents/716/2003_005_001_14249.pdf）です。リアクティブな構成と四特性の参考資料は、リアクティブ宣言（https://www.reactivemanifesto.org/ja）です。本書のTextus/CNCFとの対応表は、これらの一般的な考え方を踏まえ、関連技術ガイドの内容を品質属性の観点から整理したものです。</span><span lang="en">For quality attribute scenarios, see SEI, Quality Attribute Workshops, Third Edition (https://www.sei.cmu.edu/documents/716/2003_005_001_14249.pdf). For reactive architecture and its four characteristics, see The Reactive Manifesto (https://www.reactivemanifesto.org/). The Textus/CNCF mappings in this guide organize the related technical guides by quality attribute, informed by these general concepts.</span>

